# CPUs numbered in MPIDR Aff1 (patch 0020). DynamIQ cores, like the Q8B's
# (MPIDR 0x000-0x700), number themselves in Aff1 with Aff0 = 0. QEMU virt
# can't do that: it gives 16 CPUs per Aff1 value whatever -smp's topology
# (hw/arm/virt.c virt_cpu_mp_affinity), so 18 CPUs make cpu 16 and 17
# MPIDR 0x100 and 0x101. 0x100 has Aff0 = 0, like the boot CPU: before 0020
# start.s matched it to the boot CPU's cpu_data. Each must come up on its
# own, take IPIs addressed through ICC_SGI1R_EL1's Aff1 field, and count.
sh_test(
    name = "sbsa_a76_aff1_boot_test",
